# Health Integration Modernization (v11.0.0+ Migration)

The `health` package has been updated to version 11.0.0, which introduces significant breaking changes: the removal of the legacy Google Fit API and the shift to **Google Health Connect** on Android. The `HealthFactory` class has also been replaced by the `Health` class.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Health Connect App Requirement**: Since Google Fit support is removed, you MUST have the **Health Connect** app installed on your Android device (it is built-in on Android 14+, but might need to be downloaded from the Play Store on older versions).
> 
> **Permissions**: You will need to grant "All permissions" in the Health Connect sync settings on your phone after the first launch.

## Proposed Changes

The following changes have already been prepared/applied to ensure compatibility:

### Core Logic

#### [MODIFY] [health_service.dart](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/mobile_app/lib/services/health_service.dart)
- Migrated legacy `HealthFactory` usage to the new `Health` class.
- Added mandatory `_health.configure()` call for initialization.
- Updated `hasPermissions` and `requestAuthorization` to include explicit `HealthDataAccess` permissions required by the new SDK.
- **Added new Health Metrics**: Added support for Calories, Distance, Weight, and Water Intake.

---

### Android Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [AndroidManifest.xml](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/mobile_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml)
- Added mandatory `<uses-permission>` tags for Health Connect data types:
  - `READ_STEPS`, `READ_HEART_RATE`, `READ_SLEEP`
  - `READ_ACTIVE_CALORIES_BURNED`, `READ_DISTANCE`, `READ_WEIGHT`, `READ_HYDRATION` (New)
- Added `<queries>` tag to allow interaction with the Google Health Connect app.

#### [MODIFY] [build.gradle.kts](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/mobile_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts)
- Increased `minSdkVersion` to `26` (Android 8.0) as required by the Health Connect SDK.

